Biostimulants are agricultural products designed to support plant nutrition processes, nutrient-use efficiency, crop quality and tolerance to abiotic stress. Growing interest in resilient agriculture, efficient farm inputs and sustainable crop production is supporting demand for plant extracts, humic substances, protein hydrolysates and microbial formulations.

What Is the Biostimulants Market?
The biostimulants market includes qualifying substances and microorganisms applied to plants or soils to stimulate natural processes associated with crop development and performance. These products differ from conventional fertilizers, which primarily supply nutrients, and pesticides, which primarily control pests or diseases.

Major product categories include plant extracts, humic and fulvic acids, hydrolyzed proteins and microorganisms. They are used across fruits and vegetables, row crops, turf, ornamentals and other cultivated crops. Product selection depends on crop type, soil conditions, climate, formulation and the agronomic objective.

Key Market Drivers
Increasing Demand for Crop Resilience
Farmers face drought, salinity, temperature variation and other environmental stresses that can affect crop development. Biostimulants designed for specified abiotic stress responses are being incorporated into crop-management programs. Their use alongside irrigation, soil management and balanced nutrition may help growers address selected production challenges.

Focus on Nutrient-Use Efficiency
Growers and agricultural input suppliers are exploring products that support nutrient availability and plant nutrition processes. Biostimulants can complement conventional nutrient-management programs, creating opportunities for suppliers offering formulations supported by relevant crop trials and application guidance.

Regulatory Development and Product Verification
Defined regulatory pathways can improve transparency around product composition, claims and market access. The European Union's Fertilising Products Regulation establishes a framework for plant biostimulants, encouraging manufacturers to demonstrate product characteristics and comply with relevant requirements.

